<title>INDIA: India allocates foodgrains for April sales.</title>
<headline>India allocates foodgrains for April sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Food Ministry has allocated 1.29 million tonnes of rice and 974,000 tonnes of wheat for sale at subsidised prices through government outlets in April.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement it had allocated 1.32 million tonnes of rice and 990,000 tonnes of wheat for sale in March.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
